  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Keep your tail",
  "description": "An area of about 30 × 20 metres with a middle zone across it. Everyone has a ball and a bib tucked into their waistband like a tail. A hunter (red) stands in the middle zone.\n\nPlayers dribble through the middle zone to the other side, and back again. The hunter tries to grab the tails as players pass. Each player counts how many times they get through with their tail still on. Change hunter often. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up before you enter the zone – where is the hunter?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Change direction and pace to get past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep your body between the hunter and the ball."
    }
  ],
